The problem was a feature request to add a command that lists the disabled commands. I implemented this by adding two new subcommands to the `command_disable` group in `redbot/core/core_commands.py`:

1. `[p]command disable list`: For bot owners to list all globally disabled commands.
2. `[p]command disable list` (with alias `listdisabled`): For guild members with appropriate permissions to list all commands disabled in the current server.

These commands retrieve the list of disabled command names from the bot's configuration (global or guild-specific) and present them as a comma-separated string.

```python
    @checks.is_owner()
    @command_disable.command(name="list")
    async def command_disable_list_global(self, ctx: commands.Context):
        """List all globally disabled commands."""
        async with ctx.bot._config.disabled_commands() as disabled_commands:
            if not disabled_commands:
                return await ctx.send(_("No commands are disabled globally."))
            await ctx.send(
                _("Globally disabled commands: {}").format(
                    ", ".join(disabled_commands)
                )
            )

    @commands.guild_only()
    @command_disable.command(name="list", aliases=["listdisabled"])
    async def command_disable_list_guild(self, ctx: commands.Context):
        """List all disabled commands in this server."""
        async with ctx.bot._config.guild(ctx.guild).disabled_commands() as disabled_commands:
            if not disabled_commands:
                return await ctx.send(_("No commands are disabled in this server."))
            await ctx.send(
                _("Commands disabled in this server: {}").format(
                    ", ".join(disabled_commands)
                )
            )
```

