The problem was that the `run` command in the CLI (`src/autolabel/cli/main.py`) did not provide an option to specify an output filename, and it did not pass any output name to the `LabelingAgent.run` method. When the `LabelingAgent.run` method was called from the CLI, the `dataset` parameter was an `AutolabelDataset` object, not a string, so the default logic to generate an output name from the dataset path was bypassed, and no output file was saved.

I made the following changes:
- `src/autolabel/cli/main.py`: Added the `--output` (or `-o`) option to the `run` command. If no output name is provided, a default name is generated based on the input dataset path (e.g., `test_data.csv` becomes `test_data_labeled.csv`). This generated name is then passed to `agent.run()`.

