The issue was caused by the `Highlander` action class in `src/borg/archiver/_common.py`, which checked if an option was already set by comparing its current value in the namespace to its default value. If a user provided an option with a value identical to the default, the check would pass, allowing the option to be specified multiple times without error.

I have updated the `Highlander.__call__` method to check for the presence of the attribute in the namespace using `hasattr(namespace, self.dest)` instead of comparing values. This ensures that if an option is specified more than once, an error is raised regardless of the value provided.

```python
class Highlander(argparse.Action):
    """make sure some option is only given once"""

    def __call__(self, parser, namespace, values, option_string=None):
        if hasattr(namespace, self.dest):
            raise argparse.ArgumentError(self, "There can be only one.")
        setattr(namespace, self.dest, values)
