# Report

The issue was caused by a file descriptor leak in `filer/utils/pil_exif.py`. The function `get_exif_for_file` called `Image.open()`, which opens a file handle that remains open until the resulting image object is garbage collected. Since the image object was not explicitly closed, file descriptors were accumulating, especially in environments with many image processing operations.

I fixed this by wrapping the call to `get_exif(im)` in a `try...finally` block to ensure that `im.close()` is always called, releasing the file descriptor immediately after the EXIF data is extracted.

