The issue was caused by `RollView.get_context_data` in `will_of_the_prophets/views.py` attempting to access the `embargo` attribute of `last_roll` when no rolls exist in the database. Since `models.Roll.objects.order_by("-embargo").first()` returns `None` when the queryset is empty, the subsequent access to `last_roll.embargo` raised an `AttributeError`.

I have fixed this by checking if `last_roll` exists before accessing its `embargo` attribute. If it does not exist, `board_now` is set to `None`, allowing `board.Board(now=None)` to be called, which correctly defaults to the current time as per the `Board` class implementation in `will_of_the_prophets/board.py`.

